1. Install jenkins

#-------java dependency for jenkins------------

sudo yum install java-17-amazon-corretto.x86_64


#------------jenkins install-------------
sudo wget -O /etc/yum.repos.d/jenkins.repo https://pkg.jenkins.io/redhat-stable/jenkins.repo
sudo rpm --import https://pkg.jenkins.io/redhat-stable/jenkins.io-2023.key
sudo yum install jenkins -y
sudo systemctl enable jenkins
sudo systemctl start jenkins


2. Take the I.P address and port is 8080 e.g http://54.173.111.49:8080 and run cat command for password

3. Go to setting and selct plugins go to available plugins and select Role-based Authorization strategy and stage view and install both.

4. Go to setting and select Security in Authorization choose "role-based strategy" and save and apply.

5. Go to setting and select Users click on create user

6. Go to setting and "Manage and Assign Roles" in Role to add give any name e.g test and give requried permission click on apply and save.

7. click on Assign Roles and in Add User give username that you have created and click on the permission that you want to give to that user.

8. Go to jenkins and create pipeline from admin account and login the user account and check the permission
